BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-october-unit-backpacking@sdicscouting.org
DTSTAMP:20261010T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261012
SUMMARY:Unit Backpack Training
DESCRIPTION:Unit Backpack Training\nUNIT BACKPACK TRAINING for Troops (NOT
  for Cub Packs) is a weekend training program designed for youth so they 
 can learn basic backpacking and trail camping under their own adult leade
 rship. Backpacks\, tube tents\, and propane stoves may be provided by the
  Council for those who do not have them. This program is especially appli
 cable to those units with little or no experience or equipment. The MSR "
 T" Patch will be awarded to all participants\, youth and adult\, who succ
 essfully complete this training.\nThis weekend Backpack Training starts a
 t 8:00 Saturday morning. Backpacks\, propane fuel stoves and tube tents a
 re issued at this time. A six-mile loop trail is backpack-hiked\, ending 
 at a trail camp in MSR. High Sierra Trek-experienced instructors from the
  H.A.T. provide guidance\, instruction and help along the trail and in ca
 mp. Sunday morning will have a second short hike\, review of the trip\, a
 nd handout of patches. Scouts should be free to leave Mataguay by around 
 10:00 AM.\n\nhttps://www.sdicscouting.org/events/2026-october-unit-backpa
 cking
URL:https://www.sdicscouting.org/events/2026-october-unit-backpacking
LOCATION:Mataguay Scout Ranch\, 27955 CA-79\, Santa Ysabel\, CA 92076
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:basic-chainsaw-training-oct-2026@sdicscouting.org
DTSTAMP:20261010T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261011
SUMMARY:Basic Chainsaw Training
DESCRIPTION:Basic Chainsaw Training\nScouting America properties rely on c
 hain saws to help clear trails\, remove deadfalls\, clear timber\, and st
 ockpile wood for campfires and heating buildings. To allow for this use\,
  specific guidelines for safety have been adapted for use at all Scouting
  America activities.\nBasic Chainsaw training is a 12hr course\, it will 
 cover 3-4hr of classroom saw safety operations\, and field cutting.\nPart
 icipants will need to:\nAttend both class days to get the certification\n
 Be at least 21\nBe registered in Scouting America\nBring a current A/B ph
 ysical\nMeet at Silva Lodge @ 8 AM.\n\nhttps://www.sdicscouting.org/event
 s/basic-chainsaw-training-oct-2026
URL:https://www.sdicscouting.org/events/basic-chainsaw-training-oct-2026
LOCATION:Mataguay Scout Ranch\, 27955 CA-79\, Santa Ysabel\, CA 92070
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kayaking-merit-badge-day-2@sdicscouting.org
DTSTAMP:20261017T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261018
SUMMARY:Kayaking Merit Badge Day
DESCRIPTION:Kayaking Merit Badge Day\nScouts will have the opportunity to 
 earn the Kayaking Merit Badge\nDesigned for ages 11-17\nCost:\n$36 for yo
 uth\nLunch is NOT included. You may bring a sack lunch\nCost covers boat 
 usage fee's and Lifeguards\nCheck-in opens at 9:45 am. Class starts at 10
 :00 am.\nYouth must be pre-register. NO WALK-IN'S. | SCOUTS MUST BE ABLE 
 TO PASS SCOUTING AMERICA SWIM TEST\nPer the merit badge requirements Scou
 ts are required to pass the Scouting America swim test before attempting 
 any other requirements. Scouts will have the following options to complet
 e these requirements.\nPass Scouting America swim test day of. We ask par
 ents to stay until the scout has passed the swim test. If a scout can’t
  pass the test they will be unable to continue in the class.\nBring a pro
 perly filled out and signed Scouting America Swim Classification Record s
 heet. This must have been signed within the last year.\nIf a scout can sh
 ow proof of completing the swimming and or lifesaving merit badge within 
 the last year\, this will suffice.\nIf you have any questions please reac
 h out to\njohnathon.hall@scouting.org\nAll attending Scouts must bring a 
 Merit Badge application (\nblue card\n) with them\,\nsigned by their Unit
  Leader\n. Blue cards shall not be issued at the event. (If a Scout does 
 not bring a signed Blue Card\, the Scout may not be signed-off at the eve
 nt.)\n\nhttps://www.sdicscouting.org/events/kayaking-merit-badge-day-2
URL:https://www.sdicscouting.org/events/kayaking-merit-badge-day-2
LOCATION:San Diego Youth Aquatic Center\, 1750 Fiesta Island Rd\, San Dieg
 o\, CA 92109
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:life-to-eagle-workshop-5@sdicscouting.org
DTSTAMP:20261018T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261018
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261019
SUMMARY:Life to Eagle Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Life to Eagle Workshop\nLearn How To:\n• Choose an appropria
 te and challenging Eagle service project\n• Effectively develop and wri
 te a project proposal\n• Locate an Eagle Project Counselor/Coach\n• C
 omplete & submit the Eagle Scout Rank Application\n• Request letters of
  reference\nRSVP is required. Scouts: Life rank only. To reserve a seat a
 t one of the workshops\, send email to: doris.mccarthy@sdsu.edu. State: N
 ame of Scout\, Rank\, Unit Number\, Name of Parent\, and District. Youth 
 must copy parent when sending email to an adult. Have a copy of the Eagle
  Scout Service Project Workbook and Eagle Scout Rank Application availabl
 e – download from council website. Comfy is the appropriate dress.\n\nh
 ttps://www.sdicscouting.org/events/life-to-eagle-workshop-5
URL:https://www.sdicscouting.org/events/life-to-eagle-workshop-5
END:VEVENT
