BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-oct-unit-backpacking@sdicscouting.org
DTSTAMP:20271009T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271009
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271011
SUMMARY:Unit Backpack Training
DESCRIPTION:Unit Backpack Training\nUNIT BACKPACK TRAINING for Troops (NOT
  for Cub Packs) is a weekend training program designed for youth so they 
 can learn basic backpacking and trail camping under their own adult leade
 rship. Backpacks\, tube tents\, and propane stoves may be provided by the
  Council for those who do not have them. This program is especially appli
 cable to those units with little or no experience or equipment. The MSR "
 T" Patch will be awarded to all participants\, youth and adult\, who succ
 essfully complete this training.\nThis weekend Backpack Training starts a
 t 8:00 Saturday morning. Backpacks\, propane fuel stoves and tube tents a
 re issued at this time. A six-mile loop trail is backpack-hiked\, ending 
 at a trail camp in MSR. High Sierra Trek-experienced instructors from the
  H.A.T. provide guidance\, instruction and help along the trail and in ca
 mp. Sunday morning will have a second short hike\, review of the trip\, a
 nd handout of patches. Scouts should be free to leave Mataguay by around 
 10:00 AM.\n\nhttps://www.sdicscouting.org/events/2027-oct-unit-backpackin
 g
URL:https://www.sdicscouting.org/events/2027-oct-unit-backpacking
LOCATION:Mataguay Scout Ranch\, 27955 CA-79\, Santa Ysabel\, CA 92081
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:first-aid-adult-cpr-and-aed-oct-2027@sdicscouting.org
DTSTAMP:20271016T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271017
SUMMARY:First Aid\, Adult CPR\, and AED
DESCRIPTION:First Aid\, Adult CPR\, and AED\nSave the Date\nTopics include
 :\nAdult CPR and The Emergency Action Steps\nAutomated External Defibrill
 ator (AED) and Prioritizing Care\nUse of Barrier devices… Bleeding Cont
 rol…Tourniquets\nConscious and Unconscious Choking\, Burns and Shock\nH
 eat and Cold related emergencies and Sudden Illness\nInjuries to muscles\
 , bones and joints\nParticipants should:\nbe at least 15 years of age (ex
 ceptions can be made by training coordinator)\nbe able to complete strenu
 ous activities (such as bending\, lifting\, kneeling\, etc)\nAs a result 
 of the course\, participants will complete:\nFirst Aid and receive a 2-ye
 ar card.\nCPR and receive a 2-year card.\nThis course DOES NOT provide:\n
 First aid merit badge - Infant CPR training\nNOTE: CPR or First Aid may b
 e taken separately but the cost is the same for all or part of a class. T
 he exact start time of First Aid varies. CPR typically lasts 3 hours.\n\n
 https://www.sdicscouting.org/events/first-aid-adult-cpr-and-aed-oct-2027
URL:https://www.sdicscouting.org/events/first-aid-adult-cpr-and-aed-oct-20
 27
END:VEVENT
